---------------------------------------------------------------------------
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

                 event generator he4 - user instructions

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
usage: he4_SunOS xxx (without extension)
where xxx.inp is the input file (see in the following)

the program creates, (depending on data cards switched to 1):
xxx.hbook  -> HBOOK ntple
XXX.BOS    -> BOS file
xxx.out    -> diagnostic file
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
present energy range:  1 < w < 3.5 GeV
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
exemple of input file:

 'proton'  		! target 'proton' 'neutron' 'deuteron' 'he3' 'h3'
 7.			! laboratory beam energy (GeV)
 0.3			! E threshold for two charged in CLAS
 72.  75.		! Tagged Energy limits (% fraction of Ebeam) 
 100.			! % fraction "good"/"total" 
 0.			! energy FWHM (%)
 1,2,3,4,5,8,15,16,17,24,33,36 *
 3.0			! definition of t limit
 1			! select of distrib.(0=phasespace, 1=weighted)
 10000			! number of events
 50                     ! number of events written on control file
 103			! random number randomizer.....
 1			! BOS   output (0/1 =yes/no)
 1			! HBOOK output (0/1 =yes/no)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ATTENTION : the channel list MUST END with the symbol " * "
       IF :  jch = -1 => all proton channels are ON
       IF :  jch = -2 => all neutron channels are ON
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
=>   if you add a new channel, please update also 
=>   the reaction channel list  reported below !!!
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
related data files are read by the subroutine H_READ.F. They are:

* XTOT.MTX
contains, in 10 MeV steps, the total Xsect values according to the format:
	do j=1,251
	   read(55,*,end=335) jch
	   read(55,*) (sigr(jch,k),k=1,251)
	enddo

* CHAN_DISANG.MTX
contains, in 50 MeV steps, the differential Xsect values given in 19 
points between 0 and 180 deg (in 10 deg steps), according to the format:
      do nch=1,nchan
       read(55,*,end=333) jch
       do inw=1,50
	read(55,*) w
	read(55,*) (xchan(jch,inw,inth),inth=0,18)
       end do
      end do

* PCLE_DISANG.MTX
contains the decay angular distribution of the resonances, stored in
21 teta intervals and 41 phi intervals according to the format:
       do ith=0,20
	  do iph=0,40
	     read(55,*) th,ph,xpcle(jch,ith,iph)
          end do
       end do
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

                   INSTRUCTIONS TO ADD A NEW CHANNEL


a)........................................................................ 
ALWAYS update XTOT.MTX
The new channel must be labeled by a new "jch" value not yet used, and
the data block can be appended to the XTOT.MTX existing file.
jch label notation:
   1- 49  reaction on single nucleon (p/n)
  50-100  reaction on nucleon clusters: He3, d, diproton, ..
 101-200  risonances decay
 
b)........................................................................
IF NECESSARY, update CHAN_DISANG.MTX
if the "jch" label is not present in CHAN_DISANG.MTX, the program
automatically chooses phase-space distribution (genbod);
otherwise, it uses the subroutine GENEVT.F: in this case, ATTENTION!
  IN GENEVT.F EXTRACTED kinem values:
  REFER TO MESON for: rho-N, phi-N, omega-N, eta-N, f2-N channels
  REFER TO DELTA for: delta-N channels
  REFER TO MESON for: delta decay
  REFER TO POSITIVE MESON for: rho decay, phi decay 
  AND ARE ASSIGNED TO PARTIC #1
if the order in which particles are given in DECAY.F (see below) is
differnt, the program automatically change the internal order
BUT IT IS BETTER TO CHECK....
 
c)........................................................................
IF NECESSARY, update PCLE_DISANG.MTX
if the "jch" label is not present in CHAN_DISANG.MTX, the program
automatically chooses phase-space distribution (genbod)

d)........................................................................
ALWAYS update the subroutine H_READ.F
You must add in:
   data ichan_p/ ...... /
   data ichan_n/ ...... /
the new protone/neutrone channel.....

e)........................................................................
IF NECESSARY update the subroutine DECAY.F
inserting a new instruction block similar to:

	partic(5,0)='proton'    |
	partic(5,1)='pi-'       |  gamma + p -> p + D++ + pi-
	partic(5,2)='delta++'   |  
	numpart(5)=2            |

	partic(17,0)='neutron'  |
	partic(17,1)='pi+'      |
	partic(17,2)='pi-'      |  gamma + n -> n + pi+ + pi- 
	partic(17,3)='neutron'  |
	numpart(17)=3           |

where, for jch=N:
	partic(N,0)= target    
	partic(N,1)= 1 part. 
	partic(N,2)= 2 part. 
	..............
	partic(N,n)= n part.  
	numpart(N) = n (numer of pcle in the final state)

f)........................................................................
IF NECESSARY, update subroutine TREE.F
if some of the added new particles decay (as, e.g. delta++, rho0, eta,..)
a new instruction block similar to the following mus be inserted:

c   delta++ decay....
	if(p.eq.'delta++')    then
	   np=2
	   pf(1)='pi+'
	   pf(2)='proton'
	   return
	endif
	
c   delta0 decay....
	if(p.eq.'delta0')     then
	   nbr=2
	   br(1)=0.33
	   br(2)=0.67
	   q=rran()
	   if(q.lt.br(1)) then
	      np=2
	      pf(1)='pi-'
	      pf(2)='proton'
	   else
	      np=2
	      pf(1)='pi0'
	      pf(2)='neutron'
	   endif
	   return
	endif

c   eta decay....
	if(p.eq.'eta')        then
	   nbr=4
	   br(1)=0.39
	   br(2)=0.32
	   br(3)=0.24
	   br(4)=0.05
	   q=rran()
	   if(q.lt.br(1)) then
	      np=2
	      pf(1)='photon'
	      pf(2)='photon'
	   else if(q.lt.br(1)+br(2))  then
	      np=3
	      pf(1)='pi0'
	      pf(2)='pi0'
	      pf(3)='pi0'
	   else if(q.lt.br(1)+br(2)+br(3))  then
	      np=3
	      pf(1)='pi+'
	      pf(2)='pi0'
	      pf(3)='pi-'
	   else if(q.lt.br(1)+br(2)+br(3)+br(4))  then
	      np=3
	      pf(1)='pi+'
	      pf(2)='pi-'
	      pf(3)='photon'

	   endif	   
	   
f)........................................................................
IF NECESSARY, update both functions RMASS.F and CHARGE.F adding the values 
of mass and charge of the new particle

g)........................................................................
IF NECESSARY, update the function CHAN.F where a new "jch" value (>100)
must be assigned to the new resonance decay mode.


